				\begin{document}$$\lambda \langle {\Omega }^{2}\rangle$$\end{document}λ⟨Ω2⟩ = (2.4 ± 0.1) × 104 (meV)2, which corresponds to an EPC strength λ = 2.58 ± 0.11. These results together provide direct experimental evidence that strong EPC is responsible for the near-room-temperature superconductivity in clathrate superhydrides. Our investigation significantly advances the experimental exploration of superhydrides, and contributes to the ultrafast dynamics investigations of quantum materials under high pressures.

